From: Muhammad Jagot <MoJagotasdfgh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:03:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fork 003: Windows service mode

What: new files cmd/holyarrs/fork_service.go, fork_service_windows.go,
fork_service_other.go (golang.org/x/sys/windows/svc, already a dependency):
  holyarrs.exe service -name <service name> -config <folder> [flags]
The Service Control Manager starts it with these words; started by hand it
refuses (exit 2). -config is required; with no -addr, HOLYARRS_ADDR or
HOLYARRS_PORT it listens on 127.0.0.1 only. Stop and shutdown end the
server cleanly (25 s); a restart or exit asked for from the controls ends
the service with that code, so the service's recovery setting starts it.

Why: run under a low-rights Windows virtual service account (no password,
no logon, no desktop) instead of in a signed-in user's session.

Check: cmd/holyarrs/fork_check_003_test.go (the arguments, the 127.0.0.1
default, refusal by hand, the exit codes, the Windows side present).

Upstream files edited: none.
